        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/valverde_denver",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Valverde Neighborhood House began as an 1891 Presbyterian church before becoming a community center for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/valverde_denver",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Valverde Elementary School, built in 1924 at West Alameda and South Tejon, stands as a landmark of early 20th‑century education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/valverde_denver",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The South Platte River marks Valverde’s eastern border, and the area has faced periodic flooding, prompting ongoing mitigation efforts.",
